  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Topic 3 covers circle mensuration, triangle trigonometry, sinusoidal functions, and (AA SL) vectors in 2D. Real-world applications include navigation, surveying, and wave modelling.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Circle formulae",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\text{Circumference }=2\\pi r,\\quad\\text{Area }=\\pi r^2,\\quad\\text{Arc length }=r\\theta,\\quad\\text{Sector area }=\\tfrac{1}{2}r^2\\theta.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Triangle trigonometry",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\frac{a}{\\sin A}=\\frac{b}{\\sin B}=\\frac{c}{\\sin C}\\quad(\\text{Sine rule}).\\]\\[c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C\\quad(\\text{Cosine rule}).\\]\\[\\text{Area}=\\tfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin C.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Trigonometric identities (IB SL required)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1,\\quad\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta},\\]\\[\\sin2\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta,\\quad\\cos2\\theta=\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Vectors (AA SL)",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\[\\mathbf{v}=\\begin{pmatrix}v_1\\\\v_2\\end{pmatrix},\\quad|\\mathbf{v}|=\\sqrt{v_1^2+v_2^2},\\quad\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=u_1v_1+u_2v_2=|\\mathbf{u}||\\mathbf{v}|\\cos\\theta.\\]<p>Vector equation of a line: \\(\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{a}+t\\mathbf{b}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 3.1 — Sinusoidal model",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "The tide height (m) is modelled by \\(h(t)=3\\sin\\!\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi t}{6}\\right)+5.\\) Find: amplitude, period, max and min heights.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Amplitude \\(=3\\) m. Period \\(=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{\\pi/6}=12\\) hours. Max \\(=5+3=8\\) m. Min \\(=5-3=2\\) m.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "ibslTideCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Sinusoidal model — tide height",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A sinusoidal tide-height model h of t equals A sine of 2 pi t over P plus k",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ibslTideDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ibslTideDataPanel",
          "descId": "ibslTideDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ibslTideDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled tide heights over one full period",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "t (hours)",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "h(t)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ibslTideA",
            "label": {
              "en": "amplitude <b>A</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 1,
            "max": 6,
            "value": 3,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTideAlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Amplitude A",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibslTideP",
            "label": {
              "en": "period <b>P</b> (hours): ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 4,
            "max": 24,
            "value": 12,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTidePlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Period P",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ibslTideK",
            "label": {
              "en": "midline <b>k</b>: ",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0,
            "max": 9,
            "value": 5,
            "step": 1,
            "valueDisplayId": "ibslTideKlab",
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Midline k",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ibslMax",
            "label": {
              "en": "max height",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "8",
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "ibslMin",
            "label": {
              "en": "min height",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "2",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Defaults reproduce Worked Example 3.1 exactly. max/min \\(=k\\pm A\\) — drag any slider and the readouts update to match.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "workedExampleCard",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example 3.2 — 3D trig",
          "ar": null
        },
        "problem": {
          "en": "A vertical pole AB stands on horizontal ground. From point C, 20 m from B, the angle of elevation of A is 35°. Find the height of the pole.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>\\(\\tan35°=\\dfrac{AB}{BC}=\\dfrac{AB}{20}.\\quad AB=20\\tan35°\\approx20(0.700)=14.0\\text{ m}.\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sine rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}=\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{c}{\\sin C} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cosine rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^2=b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>In triangle ABC, \\(AB=9\\) cm, \\(BC=7\\) cm, \\(\\angle ABC=110^\\circ.\\) Find AC and the area of triangle ABC.</p><details style=\"margin-top:8px\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;font-weight:600\">Show solution</summary><div style=\"margin-top:8px\"><p>Cosine rule: \\(AC^2=81+49-2(9)(7)\\cos110^\\circ=130+43.1=173.1.\\)</p><p>\\(AC\\approx13.2\\) cm.</p><p>Area\\(=\\frac{1}{2}(9)(7)\\sin110^\\circ\\approx29.6\\) cm\\(^2.\\)</p></div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Sine rule — non-right triangle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>In triangle \\(ABC\\), \\(a=7\\), \\(b=9\\), \\(\\hat{A}=40°\\). Find \\(\\hat{B}\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(\\dfrac{\\sin B}{9} = \\dfrac{\\sin 40°}{7}\\)</p><p>\\(\\sin B = \\dfrac{9\\sin40°}{7} \\approx 0.8264\\implies B\\approx55.8°\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example-grid",
        "label": {
          "en": "Area of a triangle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the area of triangle \\(PQR\\) where \\(p=8\\;\\text{cm}\\), \\(q=11\\;\\text{cm}\\), \\(\\hat{R}=62°\\).</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> \\(A = \\tfrac{1}{2}pq\\sin R = \\tfrac{1}{2}(8)(11)\\sin62° \\approx 38.8\\;\\text{cm}^2\\)</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "<strong>Practice:</strong> A circle has radius 6 cm. A chord subtends a central angle of 80°. Find the length of the chord.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\text{chord} = 2r\\sin(\\theta/2) = 2(6)\\sin40° \\approx 7.71\\;\\text{cm}\\)",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
